WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.767
On this slide, we are focusing on read external-style data.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:08.632
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.632 --> 00:00:14.772
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:14.772 --> 00:00:18.197
Before clicking Run, predict the structure of the output.

00:00:18.197 --> 00:00:25.107
After it runs, identify the features, target, split, prediction, or evaluation result involved.

00:00:25.107 --> 00:00:30.342
Change one input carefully and explain why the result did or did not change.

00:00:30.342 --> 00:00:34.132
Machine learning is a workflow rather than a single fit command.

00:00:34.132 --> 00:00:39.617
Keep training information separate from evaluation data, compare against a baseline,

00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:43.924
and interpret model performance in the context of the real prediction problem.
